WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:02.095
- He's an American skateboarder,

00:00:02.095 --> 00:00:04.353
actor producer entrepreneur,

00:00:04.353 --> 00:00:06.207
and reality TV star.

00:00:06.207 --> 00:00:08.274
He's one of the biggest
supporters of professional

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.493
skateboarding and one of the sports most

00:00:10.493 --> 00:00:12.123
well known characters.

00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:14.207
He was labeled one of the most influential

00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:17.138
skateboarders of all time by Fox Weekly.

00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:21.305
He's Rob Dyrdek and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:27.092
- I think when it comes to understanding,

00:00:27.092 --> 00:00:30.842
tackling fear and
relentless problem solving.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.098
The reality of learning tricks,

00:00:33.098 --> 00:00:35.090
you have to try it over
and over and over and over.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.271
Keep adjusting every
little aspect of your body

00:00:37.271 --> 00:00:38.959
to ultimately get it to work.

00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:40.736
When you get it to work it's like,

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:43.302
this incredible oh my God I
can't believe I learned this

00:00:43.302 --> 00:00:46.325
and that progression
drives you even further.

00:00:46.325 --> 00:00:48.742
(rock music)

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.358
I've always been,

00:01:08.358 --> 00:01:11.983
have an idea and execute it to a fault.

00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:15.610
What I had to learn over
the last few years is

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.283
you can't do it by yourself.

00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:21.031
I really would have said years
ago I don't do it by myself.

00:01:21.031 --> 00:01:22.423
I got all these great partners

00:01:22.423 --> 00:01:24.459
but the reality of it is,

00:01:24.459 --> 00:01:28.610
I would have my hands in
so much and not delegate

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.796
properly and put in the
right verticals on how

00:01:31.796 --> 00:01:32.979
and what you want to accomplish

00:01:32.979 --> 00:01:34.005
and go out and accomplish it.

00:01:34.005 --> 00:01:37.587
I just willed everything into existence.

00:01:37.587 --> 00:01:39.767
More than anything it's about

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:43.422
what do you love to do the
most and what are you best at?

00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:46.405
Do that all the time and
then put everybody else in

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:47.571
to fill in the rest.

00:01:47.571 --> 00:01:50.128
That's what I've really been focusing on

00:01:50.128 --> 00:01:51.669
these last couple years.

00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:53.028
Make no mistake,

00:01:53.028 --> 00:01:54.977
even every person that I
want to move forward with,

00:01:54.977 --> 00:01:57.444
all I care about is your
greatest quality is that

00:01:57.444 --> 00:01:59.764
you want to get better
tomorrow than you were today.

00:01:59.764 --> 00:02:02.181
(rock music)

00:02:15.986 --> 00:02:17.611
It was that

00:02:17.611 --> 00:02:19.890
big step for me to have money to start

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:23.232
exploring different entrepreneurial,

00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:24.584
darts if you will,

00:02:24.584 --> 00:02:27.769
at a skate shop that
lasted about three months.

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:30.570
That was where I first discovered

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:32.153
stay out of retail.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.859
Started a hip hop label.

00:02:34.859 --> 00:02:36.889
Had a rap label for a little while.

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.481
That's when I really
discovered the importance of

00:02:39.481 --> 00:02:41.783
making sure your partner
that's equally as motivated

00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:44.033
and driven as you not lazy.

00:02:44.975 --> 00:02:46.225
More than that,

00:02:48.199 --> 00:02:49.782
stick in your lane.

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:52.785
Just 'cause you think
it's cool that you're a

00:02:52.785 --> 00:02:55.034
pro skateboarder and
you got a hip hop label,

00:02:55.034 --> 00:02:55.873
you don't know what you're doing.

00:02:55.873 --> 00:02:58.823
You got no business in that.

00:02:58.823 --> 00:03:01.563
In that time period I had

00:03:01.563 --> 00:03:04.925
refocused on just all things skate.

00:03:04.925 --> 00:03:07.342
(rock music)

00:03:18.647 --> 00:03:22.004
There's this air of transparency.

00:03:22.004 --> 00:03:25.171
The entrepreneurs that I love the most

00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:27.656
they'll be honest about everything

00:03:27.656 --> 00:03:30.418
and they'll tell you exactly
how it is good or bad

00:03:30.418 --> 00:03:32.946
and will just put a stake
in the ground on a opinion

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:35.187
but not drive it home.

00:03:35.187 --> 00:03:36.829
That's the stuff I respect the most.

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:39.246
(rock music)

00:03:52.174 --> 00:03:55.687
The greatest energy that
you can live in is that

00:03:55.687 --> 00:03:57.854
excitement of something
coming around the corner

00:03:57.854 --> 00:03:59.021
whether it's a

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:03.070
new job or a new moment of
something big happening.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.737
There's that energy.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.255
I've figured out how
to live in that alive.

00:04:09.255 --> 00:04:13.585
I think that becomes
incredibly motivating.

00:04:13.585 --> 00:04:16.497
Then when you see the results
of making yourself better,

00:04:16.497 --> 00:04:18.271
how much better you get

00:04:18.271 --> 00:04:21.575
and how it affects the world around you,

00:04:21.575 --> 00:04:24.121
it just gives you that
much more motivation like,

00:04:24.121 --> 00:04:25.884
if I just get better and better

00:04:25.884 --> 00:04:29.179
everything gets bigger
and stronger and better.

00:04:29.179 --> 00:04:32.800
That motivation and drive
comes from that desire

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.024
to grow and create.

00:04:35.024 --> 00:04:37.166
Where I ultimately see myself

00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:39.519
I just haven't quite got there.

00:04:39.519 --> 00:04:41.936
(rock music)

00:04:52.507 --> 00:04:56.166
For the most part I don't
take meetings before 11.

00:04:56.166 --> 00:04:58.833
I build my whole schedule around

00:04:59.851 --> 00:05:02.175
my morning and the working outside of it

00:05:02.175 --> 00:05:05.068
just so it's not compromised.

00:05:05.068 --> 00:05:06.932
The only way it really becomes compromised

00:05:06.932 --> 00:05:09.351
if you begin to schedule

00:05:09.351 --> 00:05:10.804
into your time.

00:05:10.804 --> 00:05:14.303
For me it's really important
that I really don't

00:05:14.303 --> 00:05:15.136
take a meeting.

00:05:15.136 --> 00:05:16.539
If that's shooting TV,

00:05:16.539 --> 00:05:19.542
doing voiceover doing whatever.

00:05:19.542 --> 00:05:22.077
Whatever it is it never
happens before 11 down here.

00:05:22.077 --> 00:05:24.494
(rock music)

00:05:34.858 --> 00:05:39.396
I have had so many failures
at so many levels and I think

00:05:39.396 --> 00:05:42.630
I only really started
to get it and grow up

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.842
a year and a half ago
when I finally brought on

00:05:44.842 --> 00:05:47.349
a CEO for my company.

00:05:47.349 --> 00:05:49.195
He really began

00:05:49.195 --> 00:05:53.914
to help me learn to continue
to grow and then start

00:05:53.914 --> 00:05:57.516
surrounding yourself with
mentors and really smart people

00:05:57.516 --> 00:05:59.690
that have done what you're trying to do

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.361
or what you may want to do
so you can learn from them

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.861
and that really revolutionized

00:06:05.891 --> 00:06:07.278
my entire process

00:06:07.278 --> 00:06:09.874
because before I was making
millions losing millions

00:06:09.874 --> 00:06:11.603
making millions buying this doing this.

00:06:11.603 --> 00:06:13.034
I wrote produced financed films.

00:06:13.034 --> 00:06:15.489
Lose a couple million like (mumbles)

00:06:15.489 --> 00:06:18.904
I was so driven that
it didn't matter to me.

00:06:18.904 --> 00:06:21.013
I just wanted to get things done.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:23.430
(rock music)

00:06:35.132 --> 00:06:37.576
What you never want to
do is put unrealistic

00:06:37.576 --> 00:06:39.576
expectations on somebody

00:06:40.965 --> 00:06:43.222
that you're trying to
do business with because

00:06:43.222 --> 00:06:45.138
it will strain a friendship.

00:06:45.138 --> 00:06:48.403
You got to be smart to keep people

00:06:48.403 --> 00:06:52.570
in their lane and have them
excel at what they're best at.

00:06:54.023 --> 00:06:57.422
You don't want to have someone
in your particular crew

00:06:57.422 --> 00:07:01.227
take over the accounting if
they're bad with numbers.

00:07:01.227 --> 00:07:03.776
The same way you don't
want them to do design,

00:07:03.776 --> 00:07:05.749
if they suck at designing,

00:07:05.749 --> 00:07:09.259
just 'cause you need someone
else to work on design stuff.

00:07:09.259 --> 00:07:13.485
I think in all aspects of
life it's always much funner

00:07:13.485 --> 00:07:15.031
when you surround
yourself with people that

00:07:15.031 --> 00:07:16.773
you enjoy being around.

00:07:16.773 --> 00:07:19.190
(rock music)

00:07:32.791 --> 00:07:35.874
You have to focus on always learning.

00:07:39.184 --> 00:07:41.088
It's cliche but the reality of it is

00:07:41.088 --> 00:07:43.500
is if you take action and try and fail

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:47.368
you're going to learn a lot
by the time you try it again

00:07:47.368 --> 00:07:49.715
and you will build a
foundation of experience

00:07:49.715 --> 00:07:53.430
that's going to be ultimately
the rock that allows you

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.529
to find success or follow your dreams.

00:07:55.529 --> 00:07:57.946
(rock music)

00:08:09.328 --> 00:08:11.490
I don't know if I've always though global

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:13.089
but I've always thought big

00:08:13.089 --> 00:08:17.256
and I think the difference
is now I have it so clear

00:08:18.539 --> 00:08:22.289
on what I want to do for
the next 10 years that

00:08:23.813 --> 00:08:26.506
I've slowed down because
I know I'm building this

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:27.923
great machine and

00:08:28.909 --> 00:08:31.642
it's going to take me a couple years

00:08:31.642 --> 00:08:35.635
to get it perfectly in order
before I finally turn it on.

00:08:35.635 --> 00:08:37.052
When I turn it on

00:08:39.073 --> 00:08:42.738
it will be bigger than
anything I've ever done

00:08:42.738 --> 00:08:46.002
or ever will do and will
ultimately represent my legacy

00:08:46.002 --> 00:08:48.902
and I realize that's cryptic but

00:08:48.902 --> 00:08:52.233
that's how far out I'm already

00:08:52.233 --> 00:08:54.550
prepared for what I'm doing next.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.967
(rock music)

00:09:19.006 --> 00:09:20.467
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:09:20.467 --> 00:09:21.419
I hope you enjoyed.

00:09:21.419 --> 00:09:25.424
I made this video because
Jorge Gallegos asked me to.

00:09:25.424 --> 00:09:26.867
If there's a famous entrepreneur that you

00:09:26.867 --> 00:09:28.263
